# Assemble outputs. `app/<flavour>/release/` is where AGP drops a release APK, its
# baseline profiles and `output-metadata.json` — a ~10 MB build artefact that was NOT ignored,
# so a `git add -A` in a working tree that had run `assembleRelease` committed it. Ignored now
# rather than remembered: the recurrence is one careless `add` away and the cost is a blob that
# a merge commit keeps forever.
/app/*/release/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
local.properties
.idea
.kotlin
play_config.*
keystore.*
google-services.*
build
vendor/bundle/
fastlane/report.xml
.bundle
fastlane/README.md
.env
.claude.settings.local.*
.obsidian/

# shell_gate.py is run directly; its bytecode cache is not an artefact.
documentation/mockups/__pycache__/
# Any `__pycache__`, not just the mockups' one: importing a gate module for a probe writes it
# next to that module, and one slipped into a commit that way.
**/__pycache__/
